        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: event-level determination remains blocked\n\nI verified the relevant work order and the September Pending Close cutoff, but the available records do **not** support a conclusion about a late-created event.\n\n| Requested item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine–Dekoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction ID | Not available in the accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not established |\n| Exact event-created time | Not established |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot be calculated without the event-created timestamp |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not established |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Cannot determine from available evidence** |\n\nThe accessible task records contain the work order and cost-period rows, but **no `work_order_cost_events` rows**. The supporting resource returned **“supporting records not staged”**; the corresponding dataset package returned **“source role not granted.”** No authorized release became available. This missing evidence must **not** be treated as proof that no late event occurred. The stored Pending Close timestamp does not specify a time zone.\n\n### Oracle policy\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” printed page 225 (PDF page 233)**, states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions.**\n\nTherefore, a non-exempt September transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00**, while the period remained Pending Close, should be held from staging/processing. Its event type, creation time, and recorded accounting status are necessary to assess this particular event.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The audit findings and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_63d48f786986/audit-report.json`. The report was submitted, with review state **`needs_evidence`**, not validated as complete.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
